// Local code-signing config for macOS — COPY this file to `LocalSigning.xcconfig`
// (same directory, without the `.example`) and fill in your own values.
//
// `LocalSigning.xcconfig` is gitignored, so your Apple Developer Team ID never
// lands in the public repo. The committed default is empty, which keeps the
// project team-agnostic: contributors building a signed / notarized macOS app
// just drop in their own team here. An empty value falls back to ad-hoc signing
// (fine for local debug runs).
//
// To find your Team ID: Xcode > Settings > Accounts > (your Apple ID) > the
// 10-character ID in parentheses next to the team, or developer.apple.com >
// Membership > Team ID.

// Your 10-character Apple Developer Team ID, e.g. ABCDE12345
HOLLOW_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
